speechtext:
In answer to that question I propose to quote paragraph 9 of the agency agreement for the administration of N.H.A. loans, the agreement made between Central Mortgage and Housing Corporation and the lending institution or what is called an approved lender. Paragraph 9 states:
For the making and advancing of loans, the corporation will pay to the approved lender a fee of
(i)	$100 for each loan made In respect of a house other than to a builder;
(ii)	$90 for each loan made in respect of a house to a builder;
(iii)	$80 for each loan made in respect of one or more multiple family dwellings plus $10 for each family housing unit therein but not exceeding in any event a total fee of $300 for such loan; Provided that no fee shall be payable hereunder for a loan which has been approved but on which advances are made.
